  "summary": "The First Sunday of Advent homily passes for an adult parish assembly because Christ\u2019s promise in Luke 21:28 gives a hearer afraid of judgment reason to seek his help, and the request to learn God\u2019s paths after Paul\u2019s warning about contention leads to a specific repair of a neighbor\u2019s good name. I read the speech continuously, checked its argument and attributions against the reviewed study, the 1962 Missal pp. [1]\u20132, Challoner (Luke 21, Romans 13, Psalms 24 and 84), Gregory I.1 \u00a7\u00a71\u20135, Chrysostom\u2019s Romans homily 24 and Augustine\u2019s Psalm LXXXV \u00a7\u00a710 and 12, and confirmed by TeXcount the 1,171 spoken words underlying the written estimate of 10.2\u201311.2 minutes at 105\u2013115 words per minute."
